cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "psychdsish: Keep data, R code, and outputs organized and reproducible"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hussey
    given-names: Ian
    email: ian.hussey@unibe.ch
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8906-7559"
abstract: >-
  Creates a standardised R project skeleton loosely inspired by the psych-DS
  data standard for psychological data, and checks whether an existing project
  follows the same conventions. Alongside the directory structure it generates
  Quarto templates, a README, a licence, and a .gitignore with sensible
  defaults, and adds extra conventions for reproducibility and common tidyverse
  workflows. A validator function reports whether a project follows the
  conventions and, where it does not, how to fix it.
keywords:
  - psych-DS
  - reproducibility
  - project structure
  - research data management
  - R
version: 0.2.1
date-released: "2026-07-19"
